    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# iiCompression\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "iiCompression"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 6,
      "raw": "iiCompression provides bounded, in-memory gzip operations for C++23\napplications. It has no Qt or other iiSDK dependency; its implementation uses\nzlib. Applications can compose it with independent format and storage SDKs.\nSee [the gzip contract](docs/Gzip.md) and [dependency notice](NOTICE.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 7,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "fenced_code",
      "start_line": 8,
      "end_line": 12,
      "raw": "```sh\ncmake -S . -B build\ncmake --build build\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n```\n",
      "language": "sh",
      "code": "cmake -S . -B build\ncmake --build build\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n",
      "closed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 13,
      "end_line": 13,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 14,
      "end_line": 15,
      "raw": "The default build includes the library and its tests. To build only the library,\nconfigure with `-DBUILD_TESTING=OFF`.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 16,
      "end_line": 16,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 17,
      "end_line": 23,
      "raw": "The installed CMake package exports `iiCompression::iiCompression` and the\npublic header `<iiCompression/Gzip.h>`. Installation to a local prefix is an\nexplicit step; a stage inside `build/` does not update that prefix. A fresh\nconfiguration defaults to `~/.local` when `HOME` is available and accepts an\nexplicit `CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX`, including when invoked through `install.sh`.\nThe gzip interface and implementation live together directly under `src/`;\nCMake generates a build-only forwarding header to preserve the public include.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000010",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 24,
      "end_line": 24,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000011",
      "kind": "html",
      "start_line": 25,
      "end_line": 25,
